  "note": "Recto page made of TWO stacked worked-example panels and no running prose at all, so one `full` column covering the live area 0.098-0.873 is declared. Panel 1 [0.1129, 0.1341, 0.6859, 0.4389] finishes Example 1.6 (blocks n=1,2,3); panel 2 [0.1129, 0.4481, 0.6859, 0.9371] is Example 1.7 (blocks n=4..n=8 plus Fig. 1.10) and runs off the foot of the page. Both panels sample #dbdcde in their flat interior. Each panel has the thin plain cyan #00adef bar on the inner (left) edge, recorded as decorative_image, and its own wide white-on-cyan label bar - 'EXAMPLE 1.6' and 'EXAMPLE 1.7' respectively - on the outer (right) edge at x 0.696-0.738, recorded as major_heading; two label bars on one page is why that role appears twice. Block n=2 is three stacked 'Force F_n on Q due to charge q at X = ... along XO' lines, taken by A2 as one equation, so its bbox covers all three. The 'FIGURE 1.10' caption has no A2 block and carries n: null; it is cyan #00adef on the panel grey. No footer_rule. Folio '17' in a pale cyan box in the outer margin; '2022-23' recorded as running_header."
